  "description": "replacement of roof tiles and side timber framed window",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-font-kerning:1.0pt;mso-ligatures:standardcontextual;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US&quot;&gt;The proposed replacement side dormer window, given its choice of materials, would\r\nresult in an inappropriate, unduly obtrusive and incongruous addition to the dwellinghouse,\r\nfailing to respect the character and appearance of the dwellinghouse and\r\nthe visual amenities of the West Towers Conservation Area. The proposal would\r\ntherefore be contrary to the high quality design aspiration of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D1, D3 and HC1 of The London Plan\r\n(2021), Policies GR1, HE1 and Strategic Policy 02 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041)\r\nand the relevant provisions of the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
